From 30a8aac91ce4b31fb70919a93e54ac678b1529b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] hybris: finalise linker config before `on init` starts
 vendor services

On hybris the mount-namespace machinery is compiled out
(DISABLED_FOR_HYBRIS_SUPPORT), so `enter_default_mount_ns` in `on post-fs-data`
is the only thing that swaps /linkerconfig from the bootstrap configuration to
the APEX-aware default one. That happens after `on init` has already started
servicemanager, vndservicemanager and the early vendor HALs, so those processes
link against /system/lib64/libbinder.so (kHeader 'SYST') rather than the VNDK
copy in /apex/com.android.vndk.v30 (kHeader 'VNDR').

vndservicemanager is the context manager for /dev/vndbinder, so every vendor
client's Parcel::enforceInterface() fails with

    Expecting header 0x53595354 but found 0x564e4452. Mixing copies of libbinder?

and no service can be looked up on /dev/vndbinder. In particular
android.hardware.graphics.composer@2.1-service never resolves display.qservice,
exits(1), and is restarted by init every ~5s forever, so lipstick never gets a
composer and the UI never appears. Killing vndservicemanager by hand works
around it because init then respawns it after the default linker configuration
is in place.

Bind and regenerate the default linker configuration at the end of early-init
instead. APEXes are already activated at that point (SetupFlattenedApexes() runs
in SecondStageMain before any action is processed), so the later
enter_default_mount_ns / perform_apex_config become harmless no-ops.

Verified on lenovo/karatep (MSM8937, hybris-18.1): vndservicemanager now loads
/apex/com.android.vndk.v30/lib64/libbinder.so at 13s, the composer starts once
instead of crash-looping, "Mixing copies of libbinder" disappears from logcat,
and lipstick reaches the UI at ~77s with no manual intervention.

Change-Id: I2f0a3c4d5e6b7a8091c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2
---
 rootdir/init.rc | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rootdir/init.rc b/rootdir/init.rc
index ef388a63d..455304eee 100644
--- a/rootdir/init.rc
+++ b/rootdir/init.rc
@@ -73,6 +73,16 @@ on early-init
     # Generate linker config based on apex mounted in bootstrap namespace
     update_linker_config
 
+    # HYBRIS: swap in the default linker configuration here, not at
+    # post-fs-data. The mount-namespace machinery is compiled out on hybris, so
+    # the post-fs-data switch lands after `on init` has already started
+    # vndservicemanager and the early vendor HALs, which then link the /system
+    # copy of libbinder ('SYST') instead of the VNDK one ('VNDR') and cannot
+    # talk to each other over /dev/vndbinder. APEXes are already activated
+    # here, so the later calls become no-ops.
+    enter_default_mount_ns
+    update_linker_config
+
     # These must already exist by the time boringssl_self_test32 / boringssl_self_test64 run.
     mkdir /dev/boringssl 0755 root root
     mkdir /dev/boringssl/selftest 0755 root root
